<main class="wrap" id="main">
  <section class="dev">
    <h1>One line in your form.</h1>
    <p class="lead">The script finds the fields in your form and starts in silent mode. It changes nothing until you switch a field on in the admin.</p>
    <pre class="code">&lt;script async src=<span class="s">"https://api.checkdrop.dev/v1/embed.js"</span>
        data-checkdrop-site=<span class="s">"cdp_site_…"</span>&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</pre>
    <p class="note">Copy the whole line, including the site key <code>cdp_site_…</code>, from the admin: <strong>Connections → Add website</strong>, then after mapping the fields, the step <strong>Add one line to your shop</strong>. It goes into the shared footer before <code>&lt;/body&gt;</code>. The site key is public and only works from the domain you entered for the website. On your own installation, your domain replaces <code>api.checkdrop.dev</code>. If the shop uses CSP, allow that domain for both <code>script-src</code> and <code>connect-src</code>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="blk" id="api">
    <h2>Or the API.</h2>
    <p>For checks from your own server, for example when importing orders. Send the API key in the <code>X-Checkdrop-Key</code> header and never put it in the browser.</p>
    <pre class="code">POST https://checks.example.com/v1/emails/validate
X-Checkdrop-Key: cdp_…
Content-Type: application/json

&#123; "email": <span class="s">"jan.novak@gmial.com"</span> &#125;

<span class="c">→ 200, shortened</span>
&#123; "status": <span class="s">"correctable"</span>,
  "action": <span class="s">"suggest"</span>,
  "suggestion": <span class="s">"jan.novak@gmail.com"</span>,
  "issues": [&#123; "code": <span class="s">"email.domain_typo"</span>, "severity": <span class="s">"warning"</span>, … &#125;],
  "evidence": [&#123; "source": <span class="s">"dns"</span>, "state": <span class="s">"absent"</span>, … &#125;, …] &#125;</pre>
    <p><code>status</code> is <code>valid</code>, <code>correctable</code>, <code>risky</code>, <code>invalid</code> or <code>unknown</code>. <code>action</code> recommends what to do with the value, and <code>evidence</code> shows what the result is based on. When a check cannot run, you get <code>unknown</code> with the action <code>fail_open</code> and the order should go through.</p>
    <p><strong>API key:</strong> on your own installation the installer generates it into <code>/opt/checkdrop/.env</code> as <code>CHECKDROP_PILOT_API_KEY</code>. The admin cannot create further keys yet. Keys for the hosted service are issued on request.</p>
    <div class="ep">
      <code>POST /v1/emails/validate</code><span>Format, domain typo, DNS and MX with a timeout</span>
      <code>POST /v1/phones/validate</code><span>Czech number and normalised format</span>
      <code>POST /v1/names/validate</code><span>First name and surname in one field, titles, capitalisation</span>
      <code>POST /v1/addresses/validate</code><span>Name and address, match in the RÚIAN registry</span>
      <code>POST /v1/addresses/autocomplete</code><span>Address suggestions from a local copy of the registry</span>
      <code>POST /v1/company-ids/validate</code><span>Company ID (IČO), checksum, verification in ARES</span>
      <code>POST /v1/companies/autocomplete</code><span>Company suggestions from ARES by name or IČO</span>
      <code>GET /v1/health</code><span>Server status, no key needed</span>
    </div>
    <p class="aside">The exact request and response shapes are in the <a href={OPENAPI_URL}>OpenAPI contract</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="blk" id="self-hosting">
    <h2>How to deploy Checkdrop</h2>
    <p>Checkdrop is open source. Run it on your own server for free, with the same script and API as above.</p>

    <h3>What you need</h3>
    <dl class="spec">
      <dt>Server</dt><dd>Linux (Debian, Ubuntu or similar, 64-bit) with Docker Engine and Compose v2. SSH access as root or a sudo user.</dd>
      <dt>Size</dt><dd>2&nbsp;CPU, 4&nbsp;GB RAM, 20&nbsp;GB disk. The database with addresses takes about 4&nbsp;GB.</dd>
      <dt>Domain</dt><dd>A DNS A record (and AAAA with IPv6) pointing to the server, for example <code>checks.example.com</code>.</dd>
      <dt>Ports</dt><dd>80 and 443 free and open in the firewall. The HTTPS certificate is issued over port 80.</dd>
    </dl>

    <h3>Install</h3>
    <div class="install">
      <span class="install-label">Run on the server with your domain</span>
      <div class="install-row"><code id="install-command">{INSTALL_COMMAND}</code><button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" data-copy="install-command" data-done="Copied">Copy</button></div>
      <p>The installer generates passwords and keys, starts the database, the server, the admin and the scheduled jobs, gets an HTTPS certificate and prints a one-time setup code. The server is up in about a minute. Czech addresses from RÚIAN then download in the background in 5–15 minutes depending on the server, and address checks switch on by themselves.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="install">
      <span class="install-label">Or give your AI agent this link</span>
      <div class="install-row"><code id="agent-url">{INSTALL_URL}</code><button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" data-copy="agent-url" data-done="Copied">Copy</button></div>
      <p>The guide is written for agents such as Claude Code or Codex. An agent with access to your server installs Checkdrop there, checks that it runs and hands you the admin address and the setup code. The installation runs only on your side; nothing is sent to us.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>After installing</h3>
    <ol class="setup-steps">
      <li><strong>Admin account</strong><span>Open <code>https://your-domain/sign-in</code> and create the account with the setup code. Until the first account exists, <code>sudo /opt/checkdrop/checkdrop setup-code</code> prints the code again.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Website and form</strong><span><strong>Connections → Add website</strong>: the address of the page with the form and its field mapping.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Script</strong><span>Copy the <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> line into the shop. On WordPress you can use the plugin instead.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Silent mode</strong><span>Start checking the form. Fields only observe, and the Monitor shows what Checkdrop would have caught. Customers see nothing.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Switch fields on</strong><span>When you trust the results, turn on fix suggestions field by field.</span></li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Running it</h3>
    <dl class="spec">
      <dt>Updates</dt><dd>Automatic, once a day: backup of the database and settings, update, health check, and a return to the previous version if anything fails. The admin shows the running version.</dd>
      <dt>Status</dt><dd><code>sudo /opt/checkdrop/checkdrop status</code> shows what is wrong on one screen. Manual backup: <code>sudo /opt/checkdrop/checkdrop backup</code>.</dd>
      <dt>WordPress</dt><dd>The <a href={WORDPRESS_URL}>plugin</a> adds the script without editing the theme. For your own installation, enter your server's address in it. Still a pilot release.</dd>
      <dt>Trial</dt><dd>Without a server, in a clone of the repository: <code>./checkdrop install --local</code>, then <code>http://localhost:8080</code>.</dd>
      <dt>Interface</dt><dd>Admin in English and Czech. The form script follows the page's language.</dd>
      <dt>Licences</dt><dd>Server, admin, database layer and installer under AGPL-3.0. Validation core, country packs, the form script, the API contract and the WordPress plugin under MIT.</dd>
      <dt>Address data</dt><dd>Each installation downloads the RÚIAN registry straight from ČÚZK; we don't redistribute it. RÚIAN ©&nbsp;ČÚZK, CC&nbsp;BY&nbsp;4.0.</dd>
    </dl>
    <div class="dev-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-blue" href={GITHUB_URL}><Fragment set:html={iconGithub} />View on GitHub</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={INSTALL_URL}>Install guide</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={SELF_HOSTING_URL}>Running an installation</a>
    </div>
    <p class="aside">Rather not run it yourself? We deploy Checkdrop on your server or an EU host and connect your forms. One-off, from CZK&nbsp;9,900 excl. VAT; running it for you is a monthly fee by offer. <a href="/#contact">Ask for a deployment</a></p>
  </section>
</main>

